+## Maintain corpus user layers
+
+`config/cul/*.json` is the human-edited retrieval and amendment layer. The shipped
+`config/cul/default.json` preserves the default retrieval scope and is resolved and
+frozen at run setup. Validate an edited profile with:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/cul.py check --cul <profile>
+```
+
+Use `python scripts/cul.py list`, `new`, `diff`, `apply`, or `--edit` for normal CUL
+maintenance. See [`cul.md`](cul.md) for the profile contract and editor workflow.
+
+`output/corpus/blacklist.yaml` and `output/corpus/blacklist.json` are deprecated
+compatibility assets. Runtime retrieval uses the active CUL profile and falls back to
+the legacy blacklist only when no profile is available in legacy/direct contexts. If
+that compatibility snapshot is intentionally changed, edit the YAML and regenerate
+the JSON with `python scripts/build_blacklist.py`; never edit `blacklist.json` directly.
